title: a1 Kinnect
syntax: xwiki/2.1
%%WIKI-SYNC-META%%
**Abstract.** Artifact **AT-01** instantiates the Kinnect social connection-maker across three progressive builds: a **Formative Web Proof of Concept (##sce-poc##)** that overlays an interactive chest-tablet GUI onto motion-tracked video clips of a moving Pepper robot (##idle##, ##hello##, ##yes##, ##no##, ##talk##), a **Revised Local Verification Build** that replaces cloud speech and hosted language-model calls with local speech and prepared lines to satisfy EM-01 before resident contact, and an envisioned **Summative Pepper+ Build** equipped with simultaneous speaking/listening support and hardware acceleration (TECH-18) capable of running a local LLM for the two-site longitudinal trial (ER-03).

= Artifact [AT-01] =

//The Prototype, Simulation, or other tangible Implementation evaluated this cycle. It instantiates a specific set of Use Cases and, through them, the Functions, Premises, and Claims those Use Cases carry, so they can be evaluated in a controlled Evaluation.//

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|AT-01
|Name|Kinnect social connection-maker
|Status|In Progress
|Scope|(((
Implements the connection-making workflow across **UC01** (Welcoming a newcomer and building a consent-gated profile), **UC02** (Introducing two residents around shared history or interests), and parts of **UC03** (Following up and keeping a short record) through functions **F1** (Ask first), **F2** (Suggest matches), **F3** (Introduce), **F4** (Defer sensitive topics), and **F6** (Short record):

* **Formative Pepper simulation & motion-tracked chest tablet (##web/src/components/Device.tsx##, ##web/src/App.tsx##).** Preloads five real video clips of Pepper (##pepper-idle.mp4##, ##pepper-hello.mp4##, ##pepper-yes.mp4##, ##pepper-no.mp4##, ##pepper-talk.mp4##) and uses a 160×90 offscreen canvas region-of-interest tracker (##alpha = 0.28## exponential smoothing) to track Pepper's physical chest screen across body movements and overlay a 580×406 landscape tablet GUI inside the moving bezel (with an **Enlarge Tablet** toggle for low-vision accessibility). Automatically triggers physical gestures—waving hello on greeting or introduction, nodding yes or gesturing no on participant replies, and body talk while speaking—alongside top-bar controls for **Speech rate** (##Slow 0.8×##, ##Calm 1.0×##, ##Brisk 1.25×##) and **Style** (##Warm & chatty##, ##Direct & brief##).
* **Role-play cognitive walkthrough & human-factor workarounds (##web/src/App.tsx##, ##server/intake.ts##).** Assigns role-play personas (Elena, 81, early-onset Alzheimer's; Jan, 75, newcomer with left-side hearing aid; Ria, 79, mild memory slips) with human-factor prompts—such as describing a fellow resident by visual appearance or hobby when their name is forgotten (e.g., //"the gray-haired man with the yellow cat on his shirt"// for Willem, //"light-green round glasses"// for Ans, //"dark fedora hat"// for Gerrit, //"navy-and-orange headscarf"// for Corrie)—and a built-in 6-item **Participant Feedback Form** (##logs/feedback.jsonl##) recording connection-making score, tablet legibility, preferred speech rate, preferred conversation style, perceived effect of physical gesturing, and qualitative notes.
* **Prepared consent opening, visual resident lookup & profile intake (##server/intake.ts##, ##server/lines.ts##).** Opens every conversation with prepared consent lines (##open##, ##start_yes##, ##start_no##, ##not_now##) in 10 languages (##en-US##, ##nl-NL##, ##de-DE##, ##fr-FR##, ##es-ES##, ##it-IT##, ##ro-RO##, ##pl-PL##, ##lv-LV##, ##fa-IR##), bridges forgotten names against the 7-resident directory (##RESIDENT_DIRECTORY##), displays up to four tappable resident photo tiles (##show##) on Pepper's chest tablet, and records consented interests, sensitive topics (##avoid##), and connection invitations into the local SQLite store (##server/db.ts##, ##server/store.ts##).
* **Consent-gated relationship map, per-session exchange & deterministic guard (##server/store.ts##, ##server/prompt.ts##, ##server/guards.ts##, ##server/session.ts##, ##server/verify.ts##).** Stores per-resident facts (##sensitive## flag) and pairwise states (##agreed##, ##may_offer##, ##not_again##, ##unknown##, ##offLimits##). The staged walkthrough engine (DS-01, DS-02, PS-03–PS-06, SV-01, SV-02) assembles a per-session exchange containing only consented, non-sensitive items, seals the system prompt with a SHA-256 hash (M-05), filters every utterance through a deterministic guard (30 words or fewer, ##NEVER_SAY## elderspeak/memory-quiz blocklist, no unshared item IDs, no sensitive or withheld topic keywords, plus a keyword backstop for **F4** deferrals), supports plain correction (//"I had that wrong"//, flagging the item for **ST-05**), and writes a 6-item session record (**F6**) while deleting live dialogue turns under SQLite ##PRAGMA secure_delete = ON##.

**Out of scope in the current ##sce-poc## build:** real Pepper robot hardware (TECH-01) and physical lounge navigation; **F5** (UC02-F5-PR5) agreed-meeting follow-up notes and opt-in coarse room-presence counts (TECH-03); per-item consent prompts in the legacy walk session engine (##computeNextQuestion()## asks for walk and introduction consent at the pair level rather than item-by-item); and local-only speech/LLM execution (deferred to the Revised Local Build and Summative **Pepper+** Build).
)))
|Simulation notice|(((
* **What is real in the ##sce-poc## formative build:** SQLite profile and pairwise relationship store (##node:sqlite## with ##PRAGMA secure_delete = ON##); prepared multi-language line library (##server/lines.ts##); canvas motion tracking over real recorded Pepper movement clips (##idle##, ##hello##, ##yes##, ##no##, ##talk##) with synchronized chest-tablet UI overlay; live voice input and synthesis via Google Cloud Speech-to-Text (Chirp 3) and Text-to-Speech (Gemini-TTS / Chirp 3 HD) with browser Web Speech fallback (##server/speech.ts##); live conversational intake and match suggestion via hosted Claude or Gemini (##server/llm/index.ts##); deterministic utterance guard (##server/guards.ts##), SHA-256 prompt sealing (##server/prompt.ts##), and automated trial verifier (##server/verify.ts##); and persistent JSONL participant feedback logging (##logs/feedback.jsonl##).
* **What is simulated in the ##sce-poc## formative build:** Pepper's physical body and lounge presence are represented in the browser by motion-tracked video clips of Pepper rather than a physical robot in a care home; care-home residents are role-played by peer evaluators using assigned persona cards (Elena, Jan, Ria) during the formative walkthrough; and fault-injection buttons (##Reluctant##, ##Say "not again"##, ##Correct an item##, ##Sensitive question##) simulate edge-case resident actions during staged verification.
* **What requires the envisioned Pepper+ summative platform:** Standard Aldebaran Pepper (TECH-01) cannot reliably listen while speaking or moving (due to internal motor and speaker cross-talk) and lacks onboard compute for local language models. The summative evaluation (ER-03) therefore specifies **Pepper+** (TECH-18)—combining Pepper's physical form and chest tablet with simultaneous speaking/listening support and hardware acceleration running a local LLM and speech pipeline alongside the local care-home server (TECH-04).
)))
|Premises verifiable|(((
Across the six premises in [[b1 Welcoming, introducing and following up>>doc:2 Specification.b Use Cases with Claims and Premises.b1 Welcoming, introducing and following up.WebHome]]:

* **UC02-F1-PR1 (Consent record matches resident's answer — 20/20):** **Verifiable (with scope note) on ##sce-poc##; fully verifiable on Revised Local Build.** The formative walkthrough tests private consent (##yes##, ##not today##, ##not again##, and reluctant/unclear replies re-asked once then treated as ##no##) across 5 runs per event (M-01, M-10). Note: ##sce-poc## records consent at the conversation/pair level and per-fact ##sensitive##/##avoid## flags during intake, whereas per-item sharing consent prior to each introduction is completed in the Revised Local Build.
* **UC02-F2-PR2 (No excluded pair or unconsented item enters a suggestion — 20/20):** **Verifiable on ##sce-poc##.** ##/api/matches/suggest## (##server/index.ts##) and ##buildSessionExchange()## (##server/prompt.ts##) deterministically filter out ##not_again## pairs, ##offLimits## residents, and ##sensitive## facts before any prompt or suggestion is constructed (M-05).
* **UC02-F3-PR3 (Introductions use only consented items and prepared lines — 20/20):** **Qualified at best on ##sce-poc##; fully verifiable on Revised Local Build.** In ##sce-poc##, the opening consent check and symmetric introduction (##server/lines.ts##) use prepared lines and ##server/guards.ts## blocks unconsented or sensitive items, **but** open intake turns and conversational replies call a hosted LLM (Claude or Gemini). Full UC02-F3-PR3 compliance under the strict prepared-line specification (TECH-06, TECH-07) requires the Revised Local Build, whereas ER-03 evaluates guarded local LLM generation on **Pepper+** (TECH-18).
* **UC02-F4-PR4 (Sensitive topics are deferred to a trusted person — 20/20):** **Verifiable in the ##sce-poc## session engine.** Implemented in ##server/session.ts## and ##server/guards.ts## (##containsSensitiveTopic()## keyword backstop + prepared deferral line naming the resident's trusted contact from ##server/lines.ts##, with zero follow-up probing; M-06), though omitted from the abbreviated 4-premise live presentation walkthrough table.
* **UC02-F5-PR5 (Follow-up notes and opt-in room-presence pattern match scripted schedules — 20/20):** **Not verifiable on ##sce-poc## (deferred to Revised Local Build / Pepper+).** ##sce-poc## retains the earlier garden-walk session flow and does not yet implement agreed-meeting staff notes or the opt-in room-presence counter (TECH-03, M-02, M-09).
* **UC02-F6-PR6 (Short record is complete and zero packets leave the local network — 50/50):** **Fails by design on ##sce-poc##; verifiable on Revised Local Build and Pepper+.** ##sce-poc## enforces the 6-item session record and deletes live transcripts (##PRAGMA secure_delete = ON##), **but fails the network isolation check (M-07)** because speech recognition/synthesis (Google Cloud STT/TTS) and conversational replies (Claude / Gemini) traverse external cloud APIs. Replacing these with local speech/LLM execution on TECH-04 / TECH-18 makes UC02-F6-PR6 pass.
)))
|Builds|(((
|=Build|=What changed
|**Build 1 — Formative Web Proof of Concept (##sce-poc##)**|Implemented in ##..\sce-poc\##. Browser-based simulation of Pepper with real-time canvas motion tracking (##Device.tsx##) overlaying the landscape chest-tablet GUI onto five movement video clips (##idle##, ##hello##, ##yes##, ##no##, ##talk##). Includes role-play persona cards (Elena, Jan, Ria) with human-factor prompts (visual resident identification when a name is forgotten, word-finding slips), speech rate (##0.8×## / ##1.0×## / ##1.25×##) and talk-style (##Warm & chatty## / ##Direct & brief##) controls, 6-item participant feedback logging (##logs/feedback.jsonl##), SQLite profile/relationship store (##server/store.ts##), prepared multi-language consent/introduction/deferral lines (##server/lines.ts##), deterministic utterance guard (##server/guards.ts##), SHA-256 prompt sealing (##server/prompt.ts##), and automated scenario verifier (##server/verify.ts##). Uses hosted Claude/Gemini and Google Cloud STT/TTS, so UC02-F6-PR6 fails by design on this build. Used for the formative walkthrough (5 runs per event on PR1, PR2, PR3, PR6) and the 4–6 peer cognitive walkthrough probe (CL1, CL3, CL4).
|**Build 2 — Revised Local Verification Build (EM-01 target)**|Replaces cloud STT/TTS and hosted LLM calls with local-only execution on the care-home server (TECH-04) and/or strict prepared-line dialogue (TECH-06, TECH-07), adds per-item consent release prompts (F1) and agreed-meeting / room-presence follow-up logic (F5, TECH-03), reconciles persona seed data (Elena post office counter / Jan bakery from DS-01), and applies pre-committed fixes from the formative walkthrough. Used to pass the full 20-trial (PR1–PR5) and 50-trial (PR6) staged verification (EM-01) before any care-home resident takes part.
|**Build 3 — Summative Pepper+ Build (ER-03 target)**|Envisioned physical deployment on **Pepper+** (TECH-01 + TECH-18 + TECH-04): upgrades standard Pepper with simultaneous speaking/listening support (so residents can interrupt or reply while Pepper speaks or gestures) and hardware acceleration (TECH-18) running a local LLM and acoustic feature extractor entirely inside the care home's network. Supports 15–20 minute one-to-one reminiscence and profile-building conversations, multidimensional "Vibing Algorithm" matching across topic homophily and speech cadence/response latency, conversational engagement tracking (M-21), and robot-facilitated joint icebreaker sessions evaluated alongside peer connections (M-20) and bedroom isolation time (M-22) in the 4-week two-site longitudinal study (ER-03, EM-08).
)))

